# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Placeholders only — never commit real keys.

# ─── Preview mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run the whole app on sample data with no database, so the screens can be
# looked at before Supabase exists. Set to 1 to enable.
#
# It bypasses authentication, so it is deliberately impossible to enable on a
# deployed instance: it also requires a non-production build, and both
# `next build` and `next start` set NODE_ENV=production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PREVIEW_MODE=0

# ─── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project Settings → API. The anon key is public by design — every rule that
# matters is enforced by RLS and the SECURITY DEFINER functions in
# supabase/migrations/. Never put the service_role key here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_publishable_anon_key

# ─── The assistant (server only) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic Console: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Without a key the Ask panel says it is not switched on, and nothing else in
# the app is affected. Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_: that would put the
# key in the JavaScript bundle, where anybody can read it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here

# The model. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# For a proxy or a gateway. Defaults to Anthropic.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1

# ─── Visitor analytics (all optional, all server only) ───────────────────────
# The tracker, the endpoints and the whole dashboard work with none of these
# set. What they add is reach, not function.
#
# Who may read the analytics is NOT configured here. That list lives in the
# `analytics_admins` table (migration 0010), so that the application and the
# row-level policies cannot end up disagreeing about it. Adding a colleague is
# one INSERT, with no deploy.

# IP intelligence: IPinfo, or anything with a compatible response.
# Without it, resolution falls back to reverse DNS and RDAP, which are free and
# need no key. That works — it identifies fewer visitors, which is the honest
# trade and not a fault.
# IPINFO_TOKEN=

# Paid B2B enrichment, read ONLY by the "Enrich further" button on one account.
# Never called automatically, never in a loop. Every call is written to
# `enrichment_spend` with the name of the person who caused it.
# APOLLO_API_KEY=

# Shared secret for POST /api/identify, the server-to-server identity webhook.
# With this unset the endpoint answers 404 and does not exist. Set it only if
# something is actually going to call it, and treat it like a password.
# ANALYTICS_IDENTIFY_TOKEN=

# Organisation-name substrings to always classify as hosting. Comma-separated.
# Exists so a newly spotted false positive can be patched today rather than at
# the next deploy.
# ANALYTICS_EXCLUDE_ORGS=some-new-host,another-vps-brand

# A contact address, required by some free public registries' fair-access
# policies and sent in the User-Agent. The registry lookup stays off without it.
# ANALYTICS_CONTACT_EMAIL=
# ANALYTICS_REGISTRY_LOOKUP=0

# Path to a licensed identity-graph or data-sharing co-op feed, as JSON:
# [{ "hashed_email", "full_name", "email", "title", "company", "linkedin_url" }]
# Without one, a visitor who has never interacted with us stays anonymous, which
# is a data-licensing decision rather than an engineering gap.
# ANALYTICS_COOP_FILE=

# A push the moment a server-side error is caught (see src/instrumentation.ts
# and src/lib/errors/), on top of the row it already writes to error_log.
# Without this, a caught error is only ever visible to whoever thinks to open
# /analytics/errors. A Slack "Incoming Webhook" URL works directly; most other
# chat tools' webhooks read a plain { "text": "..." } body well enough too.
# ERROR_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ─── Transactional email (optional, server only) ─────────────────────────────
# What tells somebody a voucher is waiting on them, has come back to them, or
# has been approved — and what sends an invite instead of leaving the admin to
# copy the link and relay it by hand.
#
# With BOTH of these unset, nothing is sent and nothing breaks: every send site
# is best-effort and a workflow step never fails because mail did. The invite
# screen also notices and keeps telling the admin to send the link themselves,
# rather than claiming an email went out.
#
# Resend: https://resend.com/api-keys. The from address must be on a domain
# verified in that account, or every send is refused.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# NOTIFY_FROM_EMAIL=Voucher Desk <vouchers@yourdomain.com>

# ─── Google Sheets sync (optional, server only) ──────────────────────────────
# Not required to run the app — the sync worker is not built yet. v1 shipped
# without these documented, so a fresh clone could not get sync working at all.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=voucher-sheet-sync@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nyour_key_here\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"
